00:10:03.693 --> 00:10:05.290
I appreciate it, thanks.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.090
- Doing the right thing
is the right thing, babin.

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:09.500
- I wish I had a question for you,

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.776
but I know you're gonna tell
me to just fuckin' work.

00:10:11.776 --> 00:10:13.020
(Gary laughs)

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:14.330
So I just want to tell you,

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:16.650
a year and a half ago I was
going through a hard time

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:19.563
and I started listening to you
and a couple of other dudes.

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.580
You guys helped me out along the way.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.260
So from the bottom of my heart,

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:25.620
I just want to tell you thank you.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.330
And I love you.

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:28.163
- Thank you, brother.

00:10:28.163 --> 00:10:29.157
- I'll admit it.

00:10:29.157 --> 00:10:30.050
I'm gonna work my ass off for you.

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:31.661
- It's always the answer.

00:10:31.661 --> 00:10:32.494
- Absolutely.

00:10:32.494 --> 00:10:34.070
- But the only way you
can fuckin' work hard

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:35.553
is if you actually like it.

00:10:35.553 --> 00:10:36.440
- Oh yeah.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.010
- The problem is people do things

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:40.330
that they think are gonna make them money,

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:43.100
but they don't like it and
then they can't work hard

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.340
'cause they don't like it

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:45.500
and then you can't make the money

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:46.680
if you don't work hard.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:48.010
It's a fucking vicious cycle.

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:49.550
- [Gary Voiceover] The
point of view on this

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:52.490
is the word "convince"
scares the shit out of me.

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:55.100
I've spent my whole
career talking about stuff

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:57.270
that most people don't believe at the time

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:58.950
that I start talking about it.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.960
And I have found through the last 25 years

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:03.070
that I'm way better off just continuing

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:06.000
to talk about it and
not convincing people,

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.340
but letting the market
force them into my world.

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:09.620
You would be way better off

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:11.330
if you decide to do something here

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:14.430
to go to everybody and
focus on the three people

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.700
of 418 that do it with you

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:18.940
and do it amazing for
them than to sit there

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:21.950
and try to convince people
that are never gonna go there.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:25.270
Convincing the unconvinceable
is just a terrible strategy

00:11:25.270 --> 00:11:28.060
that I see so many people
spending their time with.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:30.820
I sometimes go into a
pitch and I'm fundamentally

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:32.170
checked out within the first 10 minutes.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:34.130
I'm like, this is over.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:36.300
We're here to check a box that they wanted

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:37.690
somebody innovative to be here.

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:38.523
They're out.

00:11:38.523 --> 00:11:41.990
And what's crazy I'm not
fuckin' mad at this business.

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:43.210
I signed up for this.

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:46.000
I just am not emotional
about convincing people.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:48.810
I am thrilled to just stay alive

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:51.520
until it happens and then
look at them and say,

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:53.399
I fuckin' told you, dick.

00:11:53.399 --> 00:11:56.066
(upbeat music)

